+// spreadServers orders the outbounds for picking (Wanwire): first those of
+// the servers that look healthy, then those of a server with an outbound
+// that is demoted or that the health checks found dead (deadServers), and
+// in each group the best outbound of each server first, then the other
+// transports of those servers. The expected outbounds are then on different
+// servers while there are enough, so that one server's outage takes out one
+// of them, not all, and the place of a demoted or dead outbound goes to
+// another server before it goes to a sibling that may share its fate: when
+// a server's address is blocked, the health check of one transport fails
+// first and the others follow (seen 2026-10-16, where the h3 of a server
+// whose REALITY had just failed its check took the free place for 10 s).
